<!--Post: 7556--><!--Time: 1108573463-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7556"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Surfietx<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Surfietx<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 9:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->While Googling today, I ran across this article.  It&#39;s older and a rehash of a lot of information, but it had two items of interest...at least to me. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.detnews.com/2004/nation/0404/24/nation-132261.htm" target=_top>http://www.detnews.com/2004/nation/0404/24/nation- 132261.htm</a> <BR> <BR>1.  First, the author says that he pronounced &#34;homocide&#34; in the Fox call as &#34;home-icide,&#34; with the difference being three syllables to two.  I listened to the call many times and I can hear it both ways.  What do you all think?  Could this be another word play attempt on his part? <BR> <BR>2.  Second, it mentions the photos sent of Wegerle.  No crime scene photos were taken.  So, obviously, it must have been the killer.  The author mentions that the clothes were arranged a bit differently in each photo.  Does anyone know if these were clothes on her body or around her body?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7556-->
<!--Post: 7559--><!--Time: 1108574450-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST7559"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Topsailgrl<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Topsailgrl<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, February 16, 2005 - 9:20 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Surfietx-Check this link <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/9/462.html?1108570668" target=_top>http://www.catchbtk.com/discus/messages/9/462.html ?1108570668</a><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 7559-->
<!--Post: 9505--><!--Time: 1109541126-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9505"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ozdude<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ozdude<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 1:52 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->On KSN&#39;s web site they have video of an interview they did with Dennis in 2001. I saw/heard it on TV, I can&#39;t get the video to play from the web site. It&#39;s funny, after the fact, to listen to his voice during that interview compared to the Fox phone call...seems so easy now.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 9505-->
<!--Post: 9640--><!--Time: 1109576252-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST9640"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Johno<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Johno<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Sunday, February 27, 2005 - 11:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->The guy never made the leap to actual law enforement after WSU in 1979 instead working during his WSU years installing home security systems and then becoming a code enforement officer, the position he held until February 25th, 2005. His code enforcement position was described by someone as a &#34;Glorified dog catcher.&#34; As I theorized a wanna-be cop. His use of Home-o-cide like something from the dialog out a dragnet show illustrates how he thought of himself as a cop and how he must have practiced mannerism&#39;s and the lingo of your sterotypical cop. He probably practiced in front of a mirror, like Dinero in the movie Taxidriver.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
